cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use pulse-ep in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "pulse-ep: An open-source platform for programmatic access to multivendor electroanatomical mapping data"
abstract: >-
  pulse-ep is a Python package and web platform that parses CARTO 3
  (Biosense Webster) and EnSiteX (Abbott) electroanatomical-mapping exports
  into a relational PostgreSQL database and exposes the data via a
  JWT-authenticated REST API, a browser-based 3D viewer (Three.js / WebGL),
  and a Python toolkit for custom analyses. Values from either system are
  stored under a single vendor-neutral vocabulary, so one query spans both.
  It enables quantitative research on triangulated cardiac surface meshes —
  including geodesic distance computation, surface-area integration over
  scalar intervals, map-to-map delta fields, and reference-catheter geometry
  analysis — that are not available in the clinical mapping systems.
